    "summary": "Broking giant Aon has today urged its insurer clients to leverage the record levels of reinsurance and third-party or insurance-linked securities capital as a growth-driver, saying creative use of capital and access to all its forms is increasingly important. With a record $800 billion of reinsurance capital at June 30th 2026, a new high $144.5 billion of that being from third-party or alternative sources , Aon believes the opportunity is there for protection buyers to harness this abundance to fuel their future growth. Adding that, “As market conditions evolve, product value, capital relief and access to third-party capital are becoming increasingly important.” Aon notes that there are three priorities for reinsurance buyers, using capital creatively to support growth, aligning their risk with capital and product strategies and accelerating performance through faster, more informed decision making.",
