    "url": "https://www.carriermanagement.com/news/2026/09/03/291650.htm",
    "summary": "property/casualty insurance industry posted a much higher net underwriting gain of $31.7 billion for the first half of 2026, up from $11.6 billion the prior year. “While overall industry profitability improved in the first half of 2026, largely due to a decline in insured natural-catastrophe losses compared to the first half of 2025 following the Los Angeles wildfires, insurers’ loss experience and profitability varied widely from state to state,” said Robert Gordon, senior vice president of policy, research and international at APCIA. Net income after taxes increased 53% to $77.8 billion for the first half 2026.",
