    "summary": "Challenger Life reported that its insurance-linked securities (ILS) investments, predominantly catastrophe bonds, performed in-line with their benchmark over the last year, while the company also launched a new Bermuda life and annuity reinsurance entity named Calix Re, adding a new insurance-linked dimension for the company. With its life settlements allocation now completely wound down and its reinsurance sidecar investment having dwindled to only an AU $3 million valuation by the middle of this year, the catastrophe bond investments are the main ILS allocation for Challenger at this time. In US dollar terms, this means the total insurance-linked strategies allocation of Challenger Life rose from just under US $482 million at the end of last year, to a new valuation of just over US $508 million at June 30th 2026, with the catastrophe bond investments the sole driver given the sidecar investment declined in value slightly (this may also be in run-off).",
