    "summary": "According to Verisk, the global data analytics and technology provider, the insurance industry should be prepared to withstand an average $171 billion in annual natural catastrophe losses in any given year, according to the firm’s latest average annual losses (AAL) benchmark. This information stems from Verisk’s 2026 Global Modeled Catastrophe Losses Report, which revealed that severe thunderstorm accounts for 40% of modeled insured catastrophe risk, which is more than any other peril. The figure is up $19 billion on Verisk’s 2025 benchmark, due to continued growth in property and insured values worldwide.",
