    "summary": "Germany’s government said an investigation found that Russia is behind a failed drone attack at an airport in Leipzig last month and that the Kremlin is likely to step up hybrid aggression. “On the contrary: with the attempted attack in Leipzig, the Russian leadership has deliberately chosen to inflict further significant damage on our already severely strained bilateral relationship.” The move by German authorities marks a significant deterioration in relations between Berlin and Moscow more than four years after Russia’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine. Chancellor Friedrich Merz had said last week that the attempted drone attack on the logistics hub for deliveries to Ukraine represented a new level of hybrid warfare — and perpetrators “will pay a price.” Germany will get “a fitting response” to its decisions on closing Russian facilities, Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Maria Zakharova told the state-run Tass news service.",
