    "summary": "Brookmont Capital Management, LLC, is set to move the listing venue for its Brookmont Catastrophic Bond ETF (ILS) strategy to the Texas Stock Exchange as it hopes to onboard the first lead market maker to the fund within weeks. The Brookmont Catastrophic Bond ETF failed to secure a lead market maker for its launch, in part because the ILS asset class is difficult to hedge, but now the firm behind it is hopeful this move to a Texas Stock Exchange listing may make that a simpler process. Bid–ask spreads remained tight at around 10 basis points on a median basis, reflecting an efficient secondary market and effective support from the ETF’s authorized participants.” Powell of Brookmont further explained that the transfer of the listing to Texas is “an opportunity to continue to grow and scale ILS, facilitated by a lead market maker.”",
