    "summary": "International advertising and marketing firm Dentsu International Americas, LLC, violated federal law when it refused to hire a pregnant woman for a Minneapolis-based position promoting alcoholic beverage brands, the U.S. Such conduct violates the Pregnant Workers Fairness Act, which prohibits an employer from refusing to hire a pregnant employee because she will need a reasonable accommodation, which can include time off to recover from childbirth. According to the suit, in November 2023, Dentsu refused to hire a female applicant for a position promoting alcoholic beverage brands and instead hired a less-qualified male applicant.",
