    "id": "lets-get-real-about-non-weather-water-loss-reduction-with-iot",
    "title": "Let’s get real about non-weather water loss reduction with IoT",
    "title_original": "Let’s get real about non-weather water loss reduction with IoT",
    "url": "https://www.insurancethoughtleadership.com/lets-get-real-about-non-weather-water-loss-reduction-iot",
    "summary": "LeakBot's 65,000 years of US underwriting data proves actuarially relevant loss mitigation: mature programs cut non-weather mains-related water claims ~60%, and the $5/month all-in model delivers positive ROI across market segments. Proving a sensor prevented a claim runs into three structural problems: there’s no dated invoice for a loss that never happened, early results are skewed by anti-selection bias and poor test design, and the real benefit only emerges once a program has matured well beyond its first few months. Most IoT loss-prevention studies don’t survive actuarial scrutiny — underpowered samples, uncorrected selection bias, and hidden program costs have left carriers unable to trust the ROI case for smart-home safety programs, or to justify scaling one past a pilot.",
